 "build": {
  "id": "d4487073-cbb0-4e15-b6f4-693051d0c8bb",
  "title": "Darcoded March of the Dead [dungeon leveling]",
  "description": "[overview]\ndungeon leveling build - get march of the dead - learn how to use it - win\n\nstat prio:\nleveling: Spell Power -> Intellect -> Stamina -> Spirit\n50+: Spell Power!! -> Haste Rating! -> Intellect\n\nmana regen on gear is a nice bonus if u have mp issues\n\nminions:\ndungeons - [2x] decaying colossus> abomination> crypt fiend> skeletal warrior\nfill up with greater skeletal warrior for armour reduction\nonce u hit 60 go double bonk decaying colossus.\n\n[talents]\nMarch of the Dead - massive AoE damage ability. its clunky af tho, treat it as 4 second delay ground explosion. what helped me is placing it right below the target mobs once the tank has settled (imagine a rectangle floor spawn in front of player pawn) and dont think about how theyd walk into enemies for damage. once u get the hang of it and the hang of dungeon flow (tank pulls etc) u can anticipate where the mobs will end up. this is huge for damage.\n\nrequires 0 gear to pump serious dps. 1 or 2 MotD during a fight can easily make out 70% of ur dps, surpassing other within a blink. setting up however can be very frustrating if u have a tank that constantly moves or twitches around (mr felsworn :)). in that case gl.\nstandard single target damage rotation also hits hard when combined with Deaths Due (20% enemy hp proc).\n\n[rotation]\nbuffs:\n- grim mandate> foul mandate\n- glacial ward> fetid ward/ bone ward\n\nkeep up at all times:\n- glacial tap (if mana is buffed or u have no issues)\n- animate: skeletal archer\n- harvest plague on 1-2 enemies to spawn skeletons\n\ngeneral:\n- command: hook for interrupt (can also be used to position mobs)\n^-spec out of it once u get the decaying colossus\n- tomb king for dmg\n- plague father for defensive / all out\n- when command: undead procs use blight on high hp enemies, otherwise use lichfrost\n- runic harvest in between fights for extra resource \n- deaths due for extra dmg at low enemy health\n\n- command: undead is ur main prio for single target and filler for AoE. make sure to constantly generate runic power (crypt swarm, glacial tap, etc.). ideally u build up runic power before u activate tomb king + frenzy -> command: undead\n- march of the dead nr1 prio for AoE dmg. use glacial tap and crypt swarm to generate runic power inbetween\n\n- make sure to create frozen reliquaries and keep them on cooldown when noticing mana isnt keeping up\n- if mana is still an issue refrain from using heavy mana spenders on cd (glacial tap)\n\n[macros]\nmust have macros for undead control, lets u spam the button and control undead more like a hunter pet(ish):\n1.\n#showtooltip Undead: Assault\n/cancelaura Undead: Pacify\n/cast !Undead: Assault\n/cast Grave March\n\n2.\n#showtooltip Undead: Pacify\n/cast !Undead: Pacify\n\n3.\n#showtooltip Undead: Protect\n/cancelaura Undead: Pacify\n/cast !Undead: Protect\n/cast Grave March\n\ngood to have example: auto pet attack on decay:\n#showtooltip Crypt Swarm\n/cancelaura Undead: Pacify\n/cast !Undead: Assault\n/cast Crypt Swarm\n/cast Grave March",
